BT /F2 14 Tf 0.01 0.43 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 50 713.0 Tm (ORIGINAL ON-DISK ARCHITECTURE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 679.0 Tm (An ext3 filesystem retains ext2's primary superblock, block groups, descriptors, allocation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 662.0 Tm (bitmaps, inode tables and file-block mapping. The HAS_JOURNAL compatible feature flag) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 645.0 Tm (indicates a journal. The journal commonly resides in a specially designated inode within) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 628.0 Tm (the filesystem, although external journals are possible. Its block format, headers,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 611.0 Tm (descriptors and commit records are part of the JBD journalling subsystem.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 582.0 Tm (Ext3 directory entries still refer to inodes; inodes use familiar direct and indirect) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 565.0 Tm (pointers rather than ext4's standard extent-tree layout. Revision and extension bits) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 548.0 Tm (matter: a driver should inspect explicit feature flags, not rely on a name string or assume) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 531.0 Tm (all ext-family layouts are interchangeable. JBD journal blocks have their own endianness) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 514.0 Tm (and transaction rules.) Tj ET
