BT /F2 14 Tf 0.01 0.43 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 50 713.0 Tm (DESIGN RATIONALE AND LIMITATIONS) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 679.0 Tm (The ext3 approach prioritised backward compatibility, conservative semantics and shorter) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 662.0 Tm (restart time after power loss. This came at the cost of extra journal I/O and continued) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 645.0 Tm (dependence on older block-pointer mapping. Ext4's extent mapping, larger-volume support and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 628.0 Tm (delayed allocation were designed to address workloads ext3 could not serve efficiently.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 599.0 Tm (A journal is not a backup, immutable snapshot or comprehensive protection of user data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 582.0 Tm (Filesystem capacity and directory limits depend on selected geometry and revision; a modern) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 565.0 Tm (driver that mounts ext3 must honour the supported feature masks and carefully distinguish) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 548.0 Tm (ext3 metadata from ext4-only extensions.) Tj ET
